## Ingest Workflow

When the human says "ingest [unit identifier]":

1. Read the relevant scratch files from `scratch/`
2. Create or update pages in the appropriate content category directories
   <!-- CUSTOMIZE: list which categories get created/updated and under what conditions -->
3. Create or update `concepts/` pages for any cross-cutting ideas that emerge naturally from the content
4. Name all pages by subject using kebab-case — never include unit identifiers in subject-scoped page names
5. If a subject-scoped page with a similar name already exists, create a new page with a name that reflects what is new or different — do not overwrite
6. Remove completed items from `backlog.md` that match what was just ingested
7. Update `index.md`:
   - Add entries for any new pages created
   - Update summaries for any existing pages modified
   - Organize entries by category
8. Append to `log.md`:
   ```
   ## [yyyy-mm-dd] ingest | <unit identifier> — <brief description>
   <one or two sentences summarizing what was ingested and what pages were affected>
   ```
9. Update `README.md` — see README section below
10. Run a lint pass — see Lint section below

---

## Lint (run automatically after every ingest)

After completing every ingest, perform a health check on the wiki:

- **Orphan pages** — find pages with no inbound links from other wiki pages; add appropriate cross-references
- **Missing links** — find pages that mention a concept or subject that has its own page but does not link to it; add the link
- **Concept gaps** — find concepts or themes that appear across 2+ pages but have no dedicated `concepts/` page; create one
- **Stale content** — find claims on existing pages that newer ingests have superseded or contradicted; update or flag them
- Append a brief lint summary to the current `log.md` entry

