## README.md

Maintain `README.md` at the project root as the public-facing index.

<!-- CUSTOMIZE: describe what the README should contain for your project.
  Example:
  - A brief description of the project and its goals
  - A progress table (one row per unit, updated on every ingest)
  - A highlights section (best builds, most interesting tools, running themes) — updated every 4-5 ingests
  - Links into the wiki for depth
-->

Rules:
- Write for an external reader who has never seen this project before
- Use standard markdown links, not Obsidian wikilink syntax — GitHub must render them correctly
- Keep it scannable — tables and short bullets over long prose

---

## index.md

Maintain `index.md` as the internal navigation catalog.

- Every wiki page listed with a relative link and a one-line summary
- Organized by category with a heading per category
- Updated on every ingest — new pages added, modified page summaries updated
- This is the first file to read when answering a query

---

## log.md

Append-only. Never modify or delete existing entries.

Format:
```
## [yyyy-mm-dd] <operation> | <description>
<brief summary>

[lint] <brief lint summary if this was an ingest>
```

Valid operations: `ingest`, `query`, `lint`

